OracleScheduleFuzz
├── given a valid immutable schedule and an empty bootstrap
│   ├── it starts with cutoff zero
│   ├── it schedules the first strictly future cutoff on the buffered grid
│   ├── it advances a full interval when acceptance is exactly on that grid
│   ├── it supports maximum uint48 parameters without truncating the cutoff
│   └── it accepts a one-second interval with zero buffer
└── given an invalid immutable schedule
    ├── it rejects a zero interval for every buffer
    └── it rejects a buffer equal to or larger than the interval
